cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use stabilizer-qec in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "stabilizer-qec: a quantum error-correction simulator and decoder"
abstract: >-
  A quantum error-correction simulator and decoder in Rust, with Python bindings: circuits and
  detector error models in Stim's formats, a bit-parallel sampler, exact sparse-blossom,
  correlated and belief matching, union-find, BP and BP+OSD, window decoders for real time,
  circuit diagrams, IBM's bivariate bicycle codes, any CSS code from its checks, and lattice
  surgery. Release 2.0 adds the APIs of Stim, PyMatching, sinter, ldpc and twenty-one more QEC
  tools under their own names, Clifford+T circuits with a coherent error on every gate
  (stabilizer-rank and joint samplers), fault-tolerant compilation (tqec, Loom), resource
  estimates (Azure, Qualtran), decoding as a service, and sampling and BP on the GPU.
type: software
authors:
